    "summary": "High‑energy set with soaring He's Gone and monster Truckin' > The Other One jam",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a blistering Truckin' → The Other One sequence, an inspired He's Gone, and a sprawling Playing In The Band that stretches beyond twenty minutes. Jerry's guitar soars while Phil locks in with musical telepathy. Soundboard sources capture the band at peak form.",
    "review": "September 26, 1972 at the Stanley Theatre finds the Dead firing on all cylinders. From the opening drive of The Promised Land into a crisp Cold Rain And Snow, the first set builds momentum that explodes in the second half. A monster Truckin' → The Other One jam rolls seamlessly into an impromptu Baby Blue tease before the band launches into a twenty‑plus minute Playing In The Band, showcasing Jerry’s inventive leads and Phil’s thunderous bass. He’s Gone shines as a centerpiece with soaring guitar lines and a vocal crunch from Bob that feels both urgent and tender. The rhythm section—Bill on drums and Keith’s low‑sitting piano—keeps the groove tight while Donna adds her signature harmony in the background. The encore, a rollicking Johnny B. Goode, caps a night that remains one of the most exhilarating 1972 recordings.",
